[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114146,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 113,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "<p>Ectomesenchymal chondromyxoid tumour (EMCMT) is a mesenchymal neoplasm characterized by spindle to polygonal cells within a myxoid to collagenous stroma and usually harbouring a <em>RREB1</em>::<em>MRTFB</em>&nbsp;fusion.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-07T12:47:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114147,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 113,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8982/0 Ectomesenchymal chondromyxoid tumour</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T15:03:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114148,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 113,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T15:03:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114149,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 113,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> reticulated myxoid tumour.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T15:03:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114150,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 113,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T15:03:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114151,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 113,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>EMCMT occurs in the tongue, particularly in the anterior dorsal aspect {7726361; 25404177; 27010880; 29912715}. Less common locations include the palate {22769404; 29491357} and mandible {32372271}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T15:03:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114152,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 113,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients with EMCMT have a slow-growing, painless mass, with a duration ranging from months to years {7726361}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T15:03:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114153,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 113,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There are &lt;&nbsp;100&nbsp;reported cases in the English literature. EMCMTs occur over a broad age range, but most commonly in young adults. There is no sex predilection {7726361; 25404177; 27010880; 29912715}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T15:03:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114154,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 113,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T15:03:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114155,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 113,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Approximately 90% of tumours are defined by the fusion of <em>RREB1</em> to <em>MRTFB</em>&nbsp;(<em>MKL2</em>). This fusion product has molecular pleiotropy and is not disease-specific; it has been reported in other tumours, including biphenotypic sinonasal sarcoma {33715240}, mediastinal mesenchymal neoplasms {31991003}, and oropharyngeal sarcoma {29266774}. A minority of cases may have alternate molecular drivers, including <em>EWSR1</em> {27010880; 29912715}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T15:03:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114156,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 113,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours are generally circumscribed, lobulated, and range from 5&nbsp;to 30&nbsp;mm in diameter {7726361; 29912715}. On cut section they may be grey, tan, and/or yellow {7726361}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T15:03:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114157,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 113,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>EMCMTs have a broad morphological spectrum. They are frequently multilobulated and comprise cells arranged in sheets, fascicles, and/or reticular patterns. Less commonly they may be microcytic to cystic, or papillary {7726361; 29912715}. The margins are well demarcated but usually unencapsulated, with incorporation of surrounding muscle fibres at the periphery {7726361; 25404177; 29912715}. The cells range from spindle to stellate to polygonal, with variable eosinophilic cytoplasm and round to ovoid, monomorphic nuclei. Occasional atypia, binucleation, and pseudonuclear inclusions may be identified. Mitotic activity is usually inconspicuous. The intervening stroma may be myxoid to collagenous, and focally hyaline {7726361; 25404177; 29912715}.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>Immunohistochemistry reveals polyphenotypic differentiation. Most tumours have diffuse expression of GFAP. Other stains, such as S100, desmin, SMA, myogenin, CD56, CD57, keratin, and EMA, are typically patchy and weak {7726361; 29912715}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T15:03:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114158,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 113,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T15:03:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114159,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 113,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The presence of a <em>RREB1</em>::<em>MRTFB</em> gene fusion, in the appropriate context, may be diagnostically helpful.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T15:03:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114160,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 113,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> sheets, cords, and/or a reticular arrangement of spindle to stellate to polygonal cells; variable stroma that may be myxoid, hyaline, or collagenous.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> consistent immunohistochemistry.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T15:03:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114161,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 113,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T15:03:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114162,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 113,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most tumours have an indolent clinical course, with occasional local recurrence {7726361; 19716722}. Rarely, tumours may be locally aggressive {32372271}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T15:03:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]